===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*hwat}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*kʷos}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kʷod}}. Cognates include Old Frisian ''[[hwet]]'' (West Frisian {{m|fy|wat}}), Old Saxon ''[[hwat]]'' (Low German {{m|nds|wat}}), Dutch {{m|nl|wat}}, Old High German ''[[hwaz]]'' (German {{m|de|was}}), Old Norse ''[[hvat]]'' (Danish {{m|da|hvad}}, Swedish {{m|sv|vad}}), Gothic [[𐍈𐌰]]. The Indo-European root also led to the Latin {{m|la|quod}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|kàd}}, and Irish {{m|ga|cad}}.

