* Hwæt! Wē Gār-Dena﻿ in ġēar-dagum / þēod-cyninga ﻿þrymm ġefrūġnon / hū þā æþelingas ﻿ellen fremedon. (Beowulf lines 1-3, edited and translated by [[User:Mountebank1|Mountebank1]])
*: Listǃ We, of the [[gar]]-danes, in the [[days of yore]], have heard of [[thede]]-kings' thrim, how those [[atheling]]s did [[ellen]](-deeds).
